{#
  What provides the thing this page explains.

  A page in Ways of working, Knowledge or Standards explains one feature area, and the area is
  provided by named skills and `ki` command groups. Naming them on the page is what lets a reader
  go from understanding to doing, but typed on each page the names would drift the moment the
  harness renamed one. So the names come from the crosswalk, `src/_data/featureAreas.json5`,
  which `verify:features` checks against the vendored catalogue, and the box is rendered for any
  page whose path an area names. A page no area names renders nothing.

  It shares the provenance footer's styling: like the sources table, it is about the page rather
  than part of its argument.

  See docs/guides/developer/feature-areas.md.
#}
{%- set providedBy = null %}
{%- for area in featureAreas %}
  {%- if area.page is string %}
    {%- if area.page == page.url %}{% set providedBy = area %}{% endif %}
  {%- elif area.page %}
    {%- for path in area.page %}{% if path == page.url %}{% set providedBy = area %}{% endif %}{% endfor %}
  {%- endif %}
{%- endfor %}
{%- if providedBy %}

<aside class="prose-provenance" aria-label="Provided by">

<p class="overline">Provided by</p>

<ul>
{%- for skill in providedBy.skills %}
  <li><a href="/docs/skills/catalogue/#{{ skill }}"><code>{{ skill }}</code></a>{% if providedBy.slug == 'repository-standards' and skill in ['ki-repo-kb', 'ki-repo-kb-activities', 'ki-repo-kb-live-artifacts', 'ki-repo-kb-principal', 'ki-repo-kb-streams'] %} — Knowledge bases only{% endif %}</li>
{%- endfor %}
{%- for command in providedBy.commands %}
  <li><code>{{ command }}</code> in <a href="/docs/ki/commands/">the ki CLI</a></li>
{%- endfor %}
</ul>

{%- if providedBy.interim %}
<p>The practice on this page is written up as it works now, before its standard home is chosen.</p>
{%- endif %}

</aside>

{%- endif %}
